{
  "title": "Osteitis Pubis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3093/osteitis-pubis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 1 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteitis pubis is the inflammation of the pubic symphysis caused by repetitive trauma that most commonly occurs during sports involving repetitive kicking or hip abduction/adduction.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with localized pain over the pubic symphysis with radiographs showing osteolytic pubis with bony erosions and often times diastasis of the symphysis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is nonoperative with rest, NSAIDs and activity modification.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common in soccer, hockey, football and running",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
